# game: angry, a streaming maps client for the console
#
# name is the project: it is the block in the builder's own config that says
# where this tree's two remotes are. nothing here holds a remote.
name angry

# the lint angry holds. a repository that describes any lint describes all
# of it, so this list is the whole of it.
lint width 80
lint comments
lint exclaim
lint shout
lint paragraph 4
lint words hyperscaler enterprise-grade blazing-fast load-bearing

# the design page and the readme keep their shape. the design argues from
# what the terminal can and cannot draw, at the length that argument takes,
# and the readme's examples are pasted frames, which wrap where the frame
# wrapped. reflowing either edits the exhibit.
lint allow DESIGN.md paragraph width
lint allow README.md paragraph width rows

# the suite, as a target, so a stack build runs it the way a person does.
target test . :: go test ./...

# what this tree carries on purpose.
#
# reference/ is a copy of kingfisher's own files, taken so this project can be
# read and built without reaching into the enclave. the copies name their
# origin and their author, which is the point of a reference: a reader can see
# where the shapes came from. the design page names paths for the same reason.
#
# one test names an agent, because the case it pins came from that agent's
# review.
sweep allow DESIGN.md paths
sweep allow reference/README.md paths
sweep allow reference/hexify.py author
sweep allow cmd/angry/repl_test.go word
